From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: handle a failed power up in a reset

mhi_prepare_for_power_up() frees the device context when it fails, for
instance on a BHI offset that reads as all ones from a device that is no
longer on the bus. ath11k_mhi_stop() still calls
mhi_unprepare_after_power_down() at the next power down, which frees the
command ring again and then dereferences the NULL mhi_ctxt.

A reset after the PCIe link was lost gets there: ath11k_core_reset()
ignores the failed power up, and the next suspend that powers the device
down, the shutdown or the next reset stops MHI. Remember whether MHI was
prepared, and stop it only then.

The restart that the reset started meanwhile waits in op_start, with the
rtnl lock held, for firmware that won't come up, the full 40 s. End that
wait when the power up fails. The restart then runs to its end without
firmware, as after a crash in it, and the next suspend that powers the
device down tries again.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c | 9 ++++++++-
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mhi.c  | 8 ++++++++
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/pci.h  | 1 +
 3 files changed, 17 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c
index 2c46a1292..50e15b17b 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c
@@ -2673,6 +2673,7 @@ static void ath11k_core_reset(struct work_struct *work)
 {
 	struct ath11k_base *ab = container_of(work, struct ath11k_base, reset_work);
 	int reset_count;
+	int ret;
 
 	if (!(test_bit(ATH11K_FLAG_REGISTERED, &ab->dev_flags))) {
 		ath11k_warn(ab, "ignore reset dev flags 0x%lx\n", ab->dev_flags);
@@ -2734,7 +2735,13 @@ static void ath11k_core_reset(struct work_struct *work)
 	ath11k_hif_ce_irq_disable(ab);
 
 	ath11k_hif_power_down(ab, false);
-	ath11k_hif_power_up(ab);
+	ret = ath11k_hif_power_up(ab);
+	if (ret) {
+		ath11k_err(ab, "failed to power up for the reset: %d\n", ret);
+		/* No firmware comes up to end the wait in op_start. */
+		complete_all(&ab->reconfigure_complete);
+		return;
+	}
 
 	ath11k_dbg(ab, ATH11K_DBG_BOOT, "reset started\n");
 }
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mhi.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mhi.c
index 58109aa28..240814830 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mhi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mhi.c
@@ -446,6 +446,7 @@ int ath11k_mhi_start(struct ath11k_pci *ab_pci)
 		ath11k_warn(ab, "failed to prepare mhi: %d", ret);
 		return ret;
 	}
+	set_bit(ATH11K_PCI_MHI_PREPARED, &ab_pci->flags);
 
 	ret = mhi_sync_power_up(ab_pci->mhi_ctrl);
 	if (ret) {
@@ -458,6 +459,13 @@ int ath11k_mhi_start(struct ath11k_pci *ab_pci)
 
 void ath11k_mhi_stop(struct ath11k_pci *ab_pci, bool is_suspend)
 {
+	/*
+	 * A failed mhi_prepare_for_power_up() freed the device context, and
+	 * nothing was powered up.
+	 */
+	if (!test_and_clear_bit(ATH11K_PCI_MHI_PREPARED, &ab_pci->flags))
+		return;
+
 	/* During suspend we need to use mhi_power_down_keep_dev()
 	 * workaround, otherwise ath11k_core_resume() will timeout
 	 * during resume.
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/pci.h b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/pci.h
index 1e3005a4b..1e811245c 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/pci.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/pci.h
@@ -55,6 +55,7 @@
 
 enum ath11k_pci_flags {
 	ATH11K_PCI_ASPM_RESTORE,
+	ATH11K_PCI_MHI_PREPARED,
 };
 
 struct ath11k_pci {
